WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.358 --> 00:00:02.400
CARTER MORGAN: Today,
we're talking about I/O AI,

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:04.953
and choosing your own
journey to the Cloud.

00:00:04.953 --> 00:00:07.120
I'm Carter Morgan and welcome
to This Week in Cloud,

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:10.270
where we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:12.400
The 2021 Google
I/O Developer event

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.935
will be held virtually
from May 18 to 20.

00:00:14.935 --> 00:00:16.810
Connect with developers
from around the world

00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:19.660
at this year's virtual Google
I/O for thoughtful discussions,

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:21.550
hands-on learning
with Google experts,

00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:23.980
and a first look at our
latest developer products.

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:27.610
Don't forget to register and
check out the I/O 2021 puzzle.

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:29.350
Machine learning
plays a crucial role

00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:31.780
in surveilling and measuring
the biodiversity of wildlife

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:33.250
in a non-invasive way.

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:35.470
On this episode of
"People and Planet AI,"

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:37.760
we show you how to create
an image classification

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:40.300
app for wildlife camera chats
with the help of Dataflow

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:42.700
and Google Cloud's
AI platform, Unified.

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:44.950
Watch and learn how you can
create an application that

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:47.580
tracks wildlife biodiversity.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.410
Rather than wait for
budget alert emails,

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:51.570
you can use programmatic
budget notifications

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:54.060
to send budget updates to
your favorite comms channels

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:55.110
like Slack.

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:57.360
Check out this guide on how
to set up a Cloud function

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:59.707
and transform your budget
notifications into code.

00:00:59.707 --> 00:01:01.290
Once you're working
with code, there's

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:03.860
no limit to what you can do.

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:05.720
Choose your own Cloud Adventure.

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:08.465
You get to make choices for the
engineers at the new startup

00:01:08.465 --> 00:01:10.850
Eat and Run that specializes
in pairing runners

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:13.132
with the best food options
while they're on the go.

00:01:13.132 --> 00:01:15.590
Now that the company has gained
national attention and user

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:18.707
traffic is skyrocketing, they
need your help to succeed.

00:01:18.707 --> 00:01:20.540
Should they scale up
their back-end services

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:22.250
or speed up the delivery
of their assets?

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:24.557
The choice is up to you.

00:01:24.557 --> 00:01:26.640
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:28.900
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:31.630
Any thoughts or ideas, leave
us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:34.070
We'll see you in the Cloud.

